 up 18%. It has a transformer tender of about C$900M due to award in Q1 2027.\n- Norvane Utilities plans spending up 12%, with a C$450M tender in Q2 2027.\n- VLTX holdings' utility order intake has risen each quarter: C$610M in 2025Q4, then C$640M, C$655M and C$670M across 2026Q1 to Q3. The quarterly gains are shrinking, from +30 to +15 (C$M).\n- VLTX won 60% of the last tender round. It benefits if it holds that share.\n\n**Data centres (rising, slower):**\n- The grid connections outlook expects connection requests to grow 9% in 2027. That is slower than in 2026 because power availability limits new sites.\n- Connection requests only stand in for equipment demand. I have no data-centre order or shipment figures.\n\n**Caveats:**\n- The utility capex plans are filed intentions, not orders. The two tenders, about C$1.35B combined, are the main near-term test.\n- The data-centre finding rests on a summary only. I didn't read the connection queue report it points to.\n- The mix between utility and data-centre buyers is unchecked, so I can't weight the two.\n- Whether utilities can finance the spending is a separate question. n3's debt-market finding is \"partly\": the market is open, but only to the stronger issuers. Its equity-market finding is \"no, not reliably\". That is a risk to the utility plans.\n\nSources: n7.r1 (utilities) and n8.r1 (data centres).","ttft_ms":2350,"type":"result","duration_ms":46518,"uuid":"aea6b752-6347-45ec-8ac2-36e50a4ee3aa","ttft_stream_ms":946,"time_to_request_ms":117,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":13,"system_prompt":9,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":7,"input_attachments":28,"input_hooks":6,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":10,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":14,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":5,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":8,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":2,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":2,"request_build":4},"